{"id":"NCT06676904","title":"Neonatal Platelet Transfusion Threshold Trial","official":"Neonatal Platelet Transfusion Threshold Trial","summary":"The objective of the NeoPlaTT trial is to test whether, among extremely preterm infants born at 23 0/7 to 26 6/7 weeks' gestation, a lower platelet transfusion threshold, compared to a higher threshold, improves survival without major or severe bleeding up to 40 0/7 weeks' postmenstrual age (PMA).","conditions":["Thrombocytopenia","Neonatal","Platelet Transfusion","Infant, Newborn, Diseases","Infant, Extremely Low Birth Weight","Infant, Small for Gestational Age","Thrombosis"],"interventions":[{"type":"PROCEDURE","name":"Higher Platelet Transfusion Threshold"},{"type":"PROCEDURE","name":"Lower Platelet Transfusion Threshold"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Gestational age of 23 0/7 to 26 6/7 weeks\n* Postnatal age of \\< 48 hours\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Comfort care or withdrawal of care planned\n* Neonatal alloimmune thrombocytopenia or suspected/confirmed congenital platelet or bleeding disorder\n* Receipt of platelet transfusion\n* No receipt of Vitamin K\n* Parents/guardian decline consent","minAge":"1 Hour","maxAge":"48 Hours","sex":"ALL","healthy":true,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"PREVENTION","enrollment":2433,"start":"2025-06-13","pcd":"2031-01-31","upd":"2026-03-25","sponsor":"NICHD Neonatal Research Network","areas":["other"],"central":["Ravi M Patel, MD · 404-727-5905 · rmpatel@emory.edu","Abhik Das, PhD · 301-230-4640 · adas@rti.org"],"sites":[{"f":"University of Alabama at Birmingham","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35233","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"Waldemar A Carlo, MD"},{"f":"Stanford University","city":"Palo Alto","pr":"California","zip":"94304","s":"R","lat":37.4419,"lon":-122.143,"c":"Valerie Chock, MD"},{"f":"Sharp Mary Birch Hospital for Women & Newborns","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92123","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":"Anup Kathe